  "body": "## Result\n\nFor the fixed R439 frame-509 Boolean endpoint on `(a,b,h,c)=(33,38,468,77)`, the minimum in the scalar one-destination ADD model is exactly **3**. The endpoint changes three distinct destinations, so fewer than three scalar ADDs cannot realize it. PR #1221's three-ADD word attains the lower bound. An exact four-register CNOT census has 1, 12, 97 and 626 distinct maps at lengths 0\u20133, with exactly three target words at length 3.\n\nThe four-ADD and three-ADD integer transfers are different by exactly `2 e_468 e_33^T`; this is a Boolean endpoint result, not integer-map equality.\n\n## Relationship to concurrent work\n\nHanson Sun's open [PR #1221](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1221) provides the witness and explicitly makes no minimum claim. Concurrent [PR #1344](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/1344) independently verifies the maps, full splice, and invoice, also without claiming a minimum. This package adds the local lower bound and exact shortest-word classification; it does not repeat PR #1344's full replay.\n\n## Provenance and scope\n\n- Base commit: `bce54fb3f895cbe5cd4c0eb477c3afeed100190f`.\n- Selected conditional result stays `\u03ba = 836330098538459/500000000000000000`; the complex supplier remains binding.\n- PR #1221 head `6deda901721316fcb61c6e2a6dd6b537de183452`; parent circuit PR #973 head `c05dc72734c25dd069077157224d4dd30c6e8c19`; selected PR #589 head `a5afc8c6169ea61ba7c51dfd3cade02cc7b13b46` on PR #555.\n- Source pins and overlap notes are in `research/r439-b509-local-minimality-seed06/`.\n\nThis does not establish a shortest factorization for the full frame-509 block, reprove H1\u2013H5, establish hosted supplier admission, change the paid recursive profile, or claim a new \u03ba.\n\n## Reproduction and checks\n\n```sh\npython3 -I -O -B research/r439-b509-local-minimality-seed06/verify.py\npython3 -I -O -B research/r439-b509-local-minimality-seed06/test_package.py -v\npython3 scripts/research_package.py --package research/r439-b509-local-minimality-seed06 --check-only\n```\n\nThe verifier prints `PASS_R439_B509_LOCAL_MINIMALITY minimum=3 length3_words=3 maps=1,12,97,626 boolean_inputs=16 integer_delta=2e_h_e_a no_new_kappa`. Four focused tests pass, and the package pin check prints `PASS_PACKAGE_METADATA_AND_PINS`. Local verification used Python 3.14.7. Python 3.12 is not installed locally, so I could not run the registered Python 3.12 replay in this session.\n\n## Credit and disclosure\n\nCredit Hanson Sun (@bbMisk), PR #1221, for the three-ADD witness; Cinna Davis (@1337isnot1337), PR #973, for the 21-ADD parent; DreamingOfClouds, PR #589; and eumemic, PR #555, for the retained supplier. Prepared with substantial OpenAI Codex assistance; no human independent review is claimed. Apache-2.0.\n",
